1
00:00:09,230 --> 00:00:10,350
(Passenger Drop-off Area)

2
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:39,360
=Vow of Autumn=
=Episode 11=

3
00:01:26,620 --> 00:01:27,620
Thank you.

4
00:01:37,560 --> 00:01:38,480
Let me take you home.

5
00:01:52,579 --> 00:01:54,879
I'll head up, then.

6
00:01:55,120 --> 00:01:56,180
Get home safe.

7
00:01:57,640 --> 00:01:59,000
I'll text you when I get home.

8
00:02:00,760 --> 00:02:02,939
Eat them before they go bad.

9
00:02:35,120 --> 00:02:40,200
(Cheng A J5630)

10
00:03:31,480 --> 00:03:34,940
(Operating Room
Staff Only)

11
00:03:34,940 --> 00:03:38,420
(For External Use / OTC)

12
00:03:38,420 --> 00:03:42,160
(Staff Only)

13
00:03:47,720 --> 00:03:53,540
(Operating room
Staff Only)

14
00:04:03,780 --> 00:04:04,479
Dr. Pei.

15
00:04:05,159 --> 00:04:06,520
(ICU)
You should take a break.

16
00:04:06,599 --> 00:04:08,800
You've done several surgeries today.

17
00:04:08,840 --> 00:04:09,960
Even a machine would wear out.

18
00:04:10,199 --> 00:04:11,840
I'm fine.

19
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:13,039
You call this fine?

20
00:04:13,240 --> 00:04:14,520
You skipped lunch, didn't you?

21
00:04:16,759 --> 00:04:18,319
I've got a cookie.

22
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:19,839
Want a bite?

23
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:21,560
Thanks.

24
00:04:21,879 --> 00:04:23,279
Let me catch my breath first.

25
00:04:25,360 --> 00:04:26,620
(Hot Water / Restroom / Wards / OR)

26
00:04:26,920 --> 00:04:28,519
Make way! Hurry!

27
00:04:28,980 --> 00:04:29,899
(Nurse Station)
Move!

28
00:04:30,860 --> 00:04:31,500
Move!

29
00:04:32,279 --> 00:04:32,920
Move!

30
00:04:49,100 --> 00:04:50,459
(Is this Ms. Wen Wanqing?)

31
00:04:50,459 --> 00:04:52,180
(Your mom's in emergency care
after a crash.)

32
00:04:52,180 --> 00:04:53,420
(Please come immediately.)

33
00:04:55,079 --> 00:04:55,879
I'll be right there.

34
00:05:01,160 --> 00:05:02,800
(In Operation
Staff Only)

35
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:04,279
Are you Ms. Wen's family?

36
00:05:04,639 --> 00:05:06,639
Don't worry. The surgery is underway.

37
00:05:06,899 --> 00:05:08,139
How's my mom?

38
00:05:08,399 --> 00:05:09,519
She got into a car accident.

39
00:05:09,720 --> 00:05:12,160
(Staff Only)
Splenic rupture, massive hemoperitoneum.

40
00:05:12,240 --> 00:05:13,800
(Staff Only)
Just in time.

41
00:05:13,800 --> 00:05:14,600
She's being treated right now.

42
00:05:20,900 --> 00:05:23,140
(Staff Only)

43
00:05:24,300 --> 00:05:25,500
(In Operation
Staff Only)

44
00:05:29,920 --> 00:05:32,700
(In Operation
Staff Only)

45
00:05:42,900 --> 00:05:44,260
(In Operation)

46
00:05:47,520 --> 00:05:49,020
(Staff Only)

47
00:05:49,560 --> 00:05:51,220
Doctor, how's my mom?

48
00:05:55,399 --> 00:05:57,399
Don't worry. Everything went well.

49
00:05:57,759 --> 00:05:59,399
We've repaired her spleen

50
00:05:59,399 --> 00:06:00,800
and stopped the bleeding.

51
00:06:00,800 --> 00:06:02,560
(Staff Only)
She needs ICU observation

52
00:06:02,560 --> 00:06:03,360
overnight.

53
00:06:03,399 --> 00:06:04,480
Once stable, she'll be fine.

54
00:06:10,079 --> 00:06:11,160
Let me go change.

55
00:06:11,160 --> 00:06:12,480
I'll be back to keep you company.

56
00:06:15,280 --> 00:06:17,860
(In Operation
Staff Only)

57
00:06:23,740 --> 00:06:27,300
(Hospital)

58
00:06:53,080 --> 00:06:54,760
(Care)

59
00:07:08,680 --> 00:07:10,040
After spleen repair,

60
00:07:10,740 --> 00:07:11,620
the biggest risks

61
00:07:11,620 --> 00:07:13,199
are delayed bleeding and infection.

62
00:07:13,720 --> 00:07:15,759
The first few hours are critical.

63
00:07:17,160 --> 00:07:18,399
I've spoken to Dr. Chen,

64
00:07:18,399 --> 00:07:19,399
who's on duty.

65
00:07:19,759 --> 00:07:21,199
As long as she gets through this,

66
00:07:21,379 --> 00:07:22,360
then by five or six at the earliest,

67
00:07:22,360 --> 00:07:23,560
she can be moved out of the ICU.

68
00:07:35,300 --> 00:07:36,379
Try not to worry.

69
00:07:37,120 --> 00:07:38,519
She got here in time.

70
00:07:39,079 --> 00:07:40,279
The surgery went well too.

71
00:07:40,639 --> 00:07:42,000
She'll be fine.

72
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:51,800
Pei Yiqiu.

73
00:07:53,620 --> 00:07:55,139
I just realized

74
00:07:57,420 --> 00:07:59,060
you're all grown up.

75
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:04,439
I'm 26.

76
00:08:04,439 --> 00:08:05,639
Of course I'm grown up.

77
00:08:08,980 --> 00:08:10,439
What did you think I was?

78
00:08:16,620 --> 00:08:17,300
Nothing.

79
00:08:19,439 --> 00:08:20,899
I just feel like

80
00:08:22,480 --> 00:08:23,459
with you here,

81
00:08:24,740 --> 00:08:25,620
somehow,

82
00:08:28,399 --> 00:08:29,540
I'm not as panicked anymore.

83
00:09:00,920 --> 00:09:02,860
(Passenger Drop-off Area)
